  "id": "COMPOUND:21431 - PROTEIN:6029",
  "verbalization": "Qianhucoumarin A appears to interact with Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2 through a multi-step pathway involving Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Qianhucoumarin A targets Lysosomal alpha-glucosidase, which in turn is a target of both Phillyrin and Dehydrobruceine B. These compounds then exert their effects on Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2. The integration of these pathways implies that Qianhucoumarin A may modulate the activity of this kinase through its interaction with downstream targets, potentially influencing cellular processes that depend on the kinase's function. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Qianhucoumarin A and Serine/threonine-protein kinase D2.",
